Now clear CPython semantics for slots and del:
- del of an UNSET slot → AttributeError("a") — message is just "a".
- del of a SET slot → SUCCEEDS (resets to unset).
- Reading after del → "'S' object has no attribute 'a'".

Brevi currently: my del change raises "a" always. Wrong for set slots. Fix: in del_attr, if is_slot(n): if the slot has a value in attrs → remove it and return true; else → Err("a").

Wait, Brevi unset del gave AttributeError('a') — matches CPython. Good. Set del must remove.

Also note the read after del — attrs removal gives "no attribute". Good.

But careful with dict-live case: slot values stay in attrs, so same logic works. Modify:

